{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function injectDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/debouncer/injectDebouncer.ts#L115","children":[{"type":"text","value":"debouncer/injectDebouncer.ts:115"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An Angular function that creates and manages a Debouncer instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the Debouncer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function provides debouncing functionality to limit how often a function can be called,\nwaiting for a specified delay before executing the latest call. This is useful for handling\nfrequent events like window resizing, scroll events, or real-time search inputs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available state properties:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canLeadingExecute"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have been completed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastArgs"},{"type":"text","value":": The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup on Destroy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the function cancels any pending execution when the component is destroyed.\nUse the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const debouncer = injectDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularDebouncerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularDebouncerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularDebouncer.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularDebouncer"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst debouncer = injectDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track isPending changes (optimized for loading states)\nconst debouncer = injectDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = (e: Event) => {\n  const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement\n  debouncer.maybeExecute(target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending } = debouncer.state();","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","text":"Cleanup on Destroy","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer/injectDebouncer.ts:115](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/debouncer/injectDebouncer.ts#L115)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages a Debouncer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the Debouncer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThis function provides debouncing functionality to limit how often a function can be called,\nwaiting for a specified delay before executing the latest call. This is useful for handling\nfrequent events like window resizing, scroll events, or real-time search inputs.\n\nThe debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `canLeadingExecute`: Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `isPending`: Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function cancels any pending execution when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```ts\nconst debouncer = injectDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/AngularDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularDebouncer`](../interfaces/AngularDebouncer.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst debouncer = injectDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track isPending changes (optimized for loading states)\nconst debouncer = injectDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = (e: Event) => {\n  const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement\n  debouncer.maybeExecute(target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending } = debouncer.state();\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectDebouncer\ntitle: injectDebouncer\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer/injectDebouncer.ts:115](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/debouncer/injectDebouncer.ts#L115)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages a Debouncer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the Debouncer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThis function provides debouncing functionality to limit how often a function can be called,\nwaiting for a specified delay before executing the latest call. This is useful for handling\nfrequent events like window resizing, scroll events, or real-time search inputs.\n\nThe debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `canLeadingExecute`: Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `isPending`: Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function cancels any pending execution when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```ts\nconst debouncer = injectDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/AngularDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularDebouncer`](../interfaces/AngularDebouncer.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst debouncer = injectDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track isPending changes (optimized for loading states)\nconst debouncer = injectDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = (e: Event) => {\n  const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement\n  debouncer.maybeExecute(target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending } = debouncer.state();\n```\n"}
